out.push(usecasePost('solitaire-how-to-play-strategies', 'Solitaire: Complete Guide to Winning Every Game', stableDate('solitaire-how-to-play-strategies'), 'Guides',
  'Master Solitaire with proven strategies. Learn card arrangement techniques, when to draw from the deck, and how to maximize your win rate.',
  '<p>Solitaire is one of the most played card games in the world, but many players do not know the strategies that dramatically increase win rates. This guide covers techniques that can boost your Solitaire success from the average 20% to over 50%.</p>\n<img src="https://placehold.co/800x400/5f3dc4/ede9fe?text=Solitaire+Guide" alt="Solitaire how to play" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0">\n<h2>Understanding Solitaire Fundamentals</h2>\n<p>Solitaire (also known as Klondike) uses a standard 52-card deck. Cards are arranged in seven tableau columns, with the first column having one card, the second having two, and so on. The top card of each column is face-up. Your goal is to build four foundation piles from Ace to King in each suit.</p>\n<h3>Key Rules to Remember</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Tableau columns must be built in descending order with alternating colors</li>\n<li>Foundations are built in ascending order within the same suit</li>\n<li>You can move cards between tableau columns freely</li>\n<li>Empty tableau columns can only be filled with a King</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Essential Winning Strategies</h2>\n<h3>1. Prioritize Face-Down Cards</h3>\n<p>The single most important strategy in Solitaire is revealing face-down cards. Every move that exposes a new card increases your options and brings you closer to winning. Before moving a card, ask yourself: will this reveal a face-down card?</p>\n<h3>2. Build Evenly Across Tableau</h3>\n<p>Do not focus all your effort on one or two columns. Build all tableau columns evenly to maximize your flexibility. An unbalanced tableau leaves you with fewer options and increases the chance of getting stuck.</p>\n<h3>3. Use the Draw Pile Strategically</h3>\n<p>In draw-three mode, cycle through the draw pile completely before making final decisions. Cards you pass over will return on the next cycle. In draw-one mode, use the draw pile to find specific cards but do not rely on it excessively.</p>\n<h3>4. Empty Columns Are Gold</h3>\n<p>An empty tableau column is your most powerful asset because it can only be filled by a King. Use empty columns strategically to temporarily store cards and reorganize your tableau. Creating empty columns should be a priority.</p>\n<h2>Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Moving cards to foundations too early — cards on foundations cannot return to the tableau</li>\n<li>Ignoring the draw pile — cycling through available cards reveals crucial information</li>\n<li>Focusing on one suit — spreading attention across all suits maximizes options</li>\n<li>Giving up too early — many winnable games look impossible until you find the right sequence</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Play Solitaire Online Free</h2>\n<p><a href="/en/g/solitaire">Play Solitaire online free</a> on BrowserGamesHQ and apply these strategies. With practice, you will see your win rate climb dramatically.</p>'));

out.push(usecasePost('chess-beginners-guide-online', 'Chess for Beginners: Complete Guide to Playing Online', stableDate('chess-beginners-guide-online'), 'Guides',
  'Learn chess from scratch with this complete beginner guide. Rules, strategies, openings, and how to start winning against online opponents.',
  '<p>Chess is the ultimate strategy game, enjoyed by millions worldwide. This beginner guide teaches you everything you need to start playing confidently, from basic rules to winning strategies.</p>\n<img src="https://placehold.co/800x400/5f3dc4/ede9fe?text=Chess+Guide" alt="Chess for beginners" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0">\n<h2>Chess Rules Made Simple</h2>\n<p>Chess is played on an 8x8 board with 16 pieces per side. Each piece moves uniquely: pawns move forward one square, rooks move horizontally or vertically, knights move in L-shapes, bishops move diagonally, the queen moves any direction, and the king moves one square any direction. The goal is to checkmate your opponents king.</p>\n<h3>Piece Values</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Pawn = 1 point</li>\n<li>Knight = 3 points</li>\n<li>Bishop = 3 points</li>\n<li>Rook = 5 points</li>\n<li>Queen = 9 points</li>\n<li>King = priceless (losing it loses the game)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Opening Principles for Beginners</h2>\n<p>Follow these three golden rules for the opening: <strong>control the center</strong> with your pawns and pieces, <strong>develop your knights and bishops</strong> before moving the same piece twice, and <strong>castle early</strong> to protect your king. Do not bring your queen out too early — she becomes a target for enemy pieces.</p>\n<h3>Best Openings for Beginners</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Italian Game:</strong> 1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4 — simple and effective</li>\n<li><strong>Queen\'s Gambit:</strong> 1.d4 d5 2.c4 — controls center and develops quickly</li>\n<li><strong>London System:</strong> 1.d4 followed by Bf4 — solid and easy to learn</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Middlegame Strategy</h2>\n<p>In the middlegame, focus on <strong>piece activity</strong> — active pieces control more squares and create threats. Look for tactics like forks (one piece attacks two), pins (attacking a piece that cannot move without exposing a more valuable piece), and discovered attacks.</p>\n<h2>Endgame Fundamentals</h2>\n<p>Most beginners neglect the endgame. Key principles: <strong>activate your king</strong> (he becomes a strong piece in the endgame), <strong>push passed pawns</strong> (pawns with no enemy pawns blocking them), and <strong>use opposition</strong> to outmaneuver the enemy king.</p>\n<h2>Play Chess Online Free</h2>\n<p><a href="/en/g/chess">Play Chess online free</a> on BrowserGamesHQ. Practice against AI opponents at your skill level or challenge friends. The best way to improve is consistent play combined with study.</p>'));

out.push(usecasePost('sudoku-strategies-beginners', 'Sudoku Strategies for Beginners: Tips to Solve Puzzles Faster', stableDate('sudoku-strategies-beginners'), 'Guides',
  'Learn proven Sudoku strategies that help you solve puzzles faster and more accurately. From basic scanning to advanced techniques.',
  '<p>Sudoku puzzles seem daunting at first, but with the right strategies, anyone can solve them. This guide covers techniques from beginner to advanced that will help you solve puzzles faster and with more confidence.</p>\n<img src="https://placehold.co/800x400/5f3dc4/ede9fe?text=Sudoku+Strategies" alt="Sudoku strategies for beginners" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0">\n<h2>Understanding the Basics</h2>\n<p>A standard Sudoku grid has 81 cells arranged in 9 rows, 9 columns, and 9 3x3 boxes. Each row, column, and box must contain the numbers 1-9 exactly once. The puzzle starts with some numbers already filled in — your job is to fill the rest using logic.</p>\n<h3>Getting Started: Scanning</h3>\n<p>Start by scanning rows and columns to identify where numbers must go. Look for rows, columns, or boxes that have many numbers already filled — these are your best starting points. Use the process of elimination: if a number appears in two rows of a box, it cannot appear in the third row of that box.</p>\n<h2>Basic Techniques</h2>\n<h3>1. Sole Candidate</h3>\n<p>If a cell has only one possible number that fits, that number must go there. This is the most basic Sudoku technique and the foundation of all solving.</p>\n<h3>2. Unique Candidate</h3>\n<p>If a number can only go in one cell within a row, column, or box, that cell must contain that number. This technique often reveals placements that scanning alone misses.</p>\n<h3>3. Pencil Marks</h3>\n<p>Use pencil marks (small numbers in cells) to track possible candidates. Start with cells that have the fewest possibilities. Eliminating pencil marks as you fill numbers reveals new placements.</p>\n<h2>Intermediate Techniques</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Naked Pairs:</strong> When two cells in a row, column, or box share the same two candidates, those candidates can be eliminated from other cells in that unit</li>\n<li><strong>Hidden Pairs:</strong> When two candidates appear only in the same two cells within a unit, other candidates can be eliminated from those cells</li>\n<li><strong>Box-Line Reduction:</strong> When a candidate appears only in one row or column within a box, it can be eliminated from the rest of that row or column</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Practice Progression</h2>\n<p>Start with easy puzzles (20+ given numbers) and gradually work up to harder ones. Speed comes from pattern recognition, not faster thinking. With regular practice, you will recognize common patterns instantly and solve even difficult puzzles with confidence.</p>\n<h2>Play Sudoku Online Free</h2>\n<p><a href="/en/g/sudoku">Play Sudoku online free</a> on BrowserGamesHQ. Choose from easy, medium, hard, or expert puzzles suited to your skill level.</p>'));

out.push(usecasePost('cookie-clicker-guide-tips', 'Cookie Clicker Guide: Tips for Maximum Cookies Per Second', stableDate('cookie-clicker-guide-tips'), 'Guides',
  'Complete Cookie Clicker strategy guide. Learn optimal upgrade paths, golden cookie mechanics, and prestige strategies for maximum cookie production.',
  '<p>Cookie Clicker is the definitive idle game, combining simple clicking with deep strategic decisions. This guide covers everything from basic mechanics to advanced strategies that maximize your cookies per second.</p>\n<img src="https://placehold.co/800x400/5f3dc4/ede9fe?text=Cookie+Clicker+Guide" alt="Cookie Clicker guide" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0">\n<h2>Getting Started: The First Hour</h2>\n<p>In your first hour of Cookie Clicker, focus on <strong>buying the most efficient upgrades</strong>. The best early-game purchases are cursors and grandmas, which provide the best cookies-per-second for their cost. Always buy the upgrade that gives you the best cookies-per-second increase relative to its price.</p>\n<h3>Early Upgrade Priority</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Cursors first — they are cheap and provide solid early CPS</li>\n<li>Grandmas second — they unlock synergies with other buildings</li>\n<li>Farms — unlock plant-based synergies</li>\n<li>Mines — better CPS but higher cost</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Golden Cookie Strategy</h2>\n<p>Golden cookies appear randomly and provide powerful temporary bonuses. Click them immediately. The best outcomes are Frenzy (7x production for 77 seconds) and Click Frenzy (777x clicking power for 13 seconds). Combining Frenzy with a Building Special can multiply your production by hundreds of times.</p>\n<h3>Golden Cookie Combos</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Frenzy + Building Special:</strong> Massive production boost</li>\n<li><strong>Click Frenzy + Frenzy:</strong> Thousands of times clicking power</li>\n<li><strong>Dragonflight:</strong> Extreme clicking boost for golden cookie chains</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Building Synergies</h2>\n<p>Each building type has synergies with others. Grandmas get bonuses from every other building type. Farms unlock synergies with plants. Temples and wizard towers unlock special mechanics. Understanding these synergies lets you optimize your building mix beyond simple CPS calculations.</p>\n<h2>Prestige and Progression</h2>\n<p>Once you accumulate enough prestige levels, consider resetting through ascension. Prestige upgrades provide permanent bonuses that carry over between resets. The optimal time to ascend is when you have accumulated enough prestige to buy significant upgrades — typically after your first few days of play.</p>\n<h2>Play Cookie Clicker Online Free</h2>\n<p><a href="/en/g/cookie-clicker">Play Cookie Clicker online free</a> on BrowserGamesHQ. Start your baking empire and discover why millions of players are addicted to this deceptively deep idle game.</p>'));

out.push(usecasePost('geoguessr-tips-tricks', 'Geoguessr Tips and Tricks: Become a Geography Detective', stableDate('geoguessr-tips-tricks'), 'Guides',
  'Master Geoguessr with expert tips. Learn to read landscapes, identify countries by road signs, and recognize regional architecture.',
  '<p>Geoguessr drops you into a random location on Google Street View and challenges you to guess where you are. With the right observational skills, you can narrow down locations with surprising accuracy.</p>\n<img src="https://placehold.co/800x400/5f3dc4/ede9fe?text=Geoguessr+Tips" alt="Geoguessr tips" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0">\n<h2>Instant Clues: What to Look For First</h2>\n<p>When a round starts, quickly scan for these instant clues. <strong>Language on signs</strong> is the fastest way to identify a country or region. <strong>Driving side</strong> (left vs right) eliminates half the worlds countries immediately. <strong>Sun position</strong> tells you which hemisphere you are in when combined with the time of day shown.</p>\n<h3>Priority Checklist</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Language on signs, billboards, and storefronts</li>\n<li>Which side of the road cars drive on</li>\n<li>Sun position to determine hemisphere</li>\n<li>Power pole and utility infrastructure styles</li>\n<li>Road marking colors and patterns</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Regional Identification Guide</h2>\n<h3>Europe</h3>\n<p>Europe is characterized by older architecture, narrow roads, and frequent signage. Northern Europe has distinct barn styles and vegetation. Southern Europe has Mediterranean plants and distinctive architecture. Eastern Europe has Cyrillic or other non-Latin scripts.</p>\n<h3>North America</h3>\n<p>The United States has yellow road lines, large road signs, and distinctive mailboxes. Canada has bilingual signs (English and French). Both have characteristic utility poles with multiple crossbars.</p>\n<h3>South America</h3>\n<p>Tropical vegetation, Spanish or Portuguese language, and distinctive architecture. Google car coverage is more limited but growing. Bolivia and Peru have distinctive Andean geography.</p>\n<h3>Asia</h3>\n<p>Dense urban environments in Japan, South Korea, and Taiwan. Distinctive script (Kanji, Hangul, etc.). Southeast Asia has tropical vegetation and distinctive motorbike traffic patterns.</p>\n<h3>Australia and New Zealand</h3>\n<p>Left-side driving, distinctive vegetation (eucalyptus), red soil in Australia, and characteristic mailboxes and road signage.</p>\n<h2>Advanced Meta-Strategies</h2>\n<p>Google car generation tells you when the imagery was captured. Google car color varies by region. Street View coverage gaps tell you where you are not. The presence of blurring on faces and license plates is universal but the specific blurring pattern differs by region.</p>\n<h2>Practice and Improve</h2>\n<p>The best way to improve at Geoguessr is to play consistently and review your mistakes. Study one region at a time rather than trying to learn everything at once. Focus on developing a systematic observation process that you apply to every round.</p>\n<h2>Play Geoguessr Online Free</h2>\n<p><a href="/en/g/geoguessr">Play Geoguessr online free</a> on BrowserGamesHQ. Explore the world and test your geography knowledge.</p>'));

out.push(usecasePost('tetris-tips-high-score', 'Tetris Tips: How to Get High Scores and Survive Longer', stableDate('tetris-tips-high-score'), 'Guides',
  'Master Tetris with proven strategies. Learn stacking techniques, T-spin setups, and speed-building methods for marathon mode.',
  '<p>Tetris has captivated players for decades with its perfect blend of simple mechanics and deep strategy. This guide covers techniques that will dramatically improve your scores and survival time.</p>\n<img src="https://placehold.co/800x400/5f3dc4/ede9fe?text=Tetris+Tips" alt="Tetris tips" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0">\n<h2>Fundamental Stacking</h2>\n<p>The foundation of good Tetris is <strong>flat stacking</strong>. Keep your stack as flat as possible by filling gaps immediately. A flat stack gives you more options and more time to react as speed increases. Avoid creating columns that are significantly taller than others.</p>\n<h3>Flat Stacking Principles</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fill gaps as soon as they appear — do not leave holes</li>\n<li>Keep the stack level across all columns</li>\n<li>Avoid creating single-column valleys that are hard to fill</li>\n<li>Use pieces in the order they arrive, do not hold pieces unnecessarily</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>The 4-Line Clear (Tetris)</h2>\n<p>Clearing four lines at once with an I-piece is the most efficient scoring method. Set up your stack so that only one column remains open, then drop the I-piece when it arrives. This requires keeping your stack exactly 9 columns wide and waiting for the I-piece, but the score bonus makes it worthwhile.</p>\n<h2>T-Spin Techniques</h2>\n<p>Advanced players score more through T-spins than through Tetris clears. A T-spin occurs when you rotate a T-piece into a tight space. T-spin doubles and triples provide enormous score bonuses and are the key to competitive Tetris scoring. Practice basic T-spin setups in slow practice mode before attempting them at speed.</p>\n<h3>T-Spin Setup Types</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>T-Spin Single:</strong> Basic T-spin that clears one line</li>\n<li><strong>T-Spin Double:</strong> Clears two lines — the most efficient T-spin</li>\n<li><strong>T-Spin Triple:</strong> Clears three lines — difficult but massively rewarding</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Managing Increasing Speed</h2>\n<p>As speed increases, simplify your strategy. At high speeds, do not attempt complex T-spin setups — focus on flat stacking and quick decisions. Use the hold piece strategically to keep an I-piece for emergencies. Anticipate your next pieces using the preview window.</p>\n<h2>Practice Regimen</h2>\n<p>Start with marathon mode at slow speeds. Focus only on flat stacking for your first 10 games. Then add T-spin practice for 10 games. Finally, combine both techniques in full games. Consistent daily practice of 15-20 minutes produces faster improvement than occasional marathon sessions.</p>\n<h2>Play Tetris Online Free</h2>\n<p><a href="/en/g/tetris">Play Tetris online free</a> on BrowserGamesHQ and apply these strategies to achieve new high scores.</p>'));

out.push(usecasePost('wordle-tips-daily-puzzle', 'Wordle Tips: How to Solve the Daily Puzzle Every Time', stableDate('wordle-tips-daily-puzzle'), 'Guides',
  'Master Wordle with proven starting words and deduction strategies. Solve the daily puzzle in 3-4 guesses consistently.',
  '<p>Wordle has become a daily ritual for millions of players. While luck plays a role, strategic play dramatically improves your solving rate. This guide covers optimal starting words and deduction strategies that help you solve the puzzle in 3-4 guesses consistently.</p>\n<img src="https://placehold.co/800x400/5f3dc4/ede9fe?text=Wordle+Tips" alt="Wordle tips" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0">\n<h2>Optimal Starting Words</h2>\n<p>Your first guess is the most important decision in Wordle. The best starting words use common letters and cover multiple vowels. Research shows that certain words eliminate the most possibilities on average.</p>\n<h3>Best Starting Words</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>CRANE</strong> — statistically the best opening word, covering C, R, A, N, E</li>\n<li><strong>SLATE</strong> — excellent coverage of common consonants and vowels</li>\n<li><strong>AUDIO</strong> — covers four vowels, maximizing vowel information</li>\n<li><strong>ADIEU</strong> — another strong vowel-focused opener</li>\n<li><strong>STARE</strong> — strong consonant coverage with common letters</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Information Maximization</h2>\n<p>Each guess should maximize the information you gain, not just try to solve the puzzle. A guess that confirms several letters is better than a guess that might solve it but provides little information if wrong. Use your second guess to test multiple new letters that could fit the pattern revealed by your first guess.</p>\n<h3>Letter Frequency Knowledge</h3>\n<p>The most common English letters are E, A, R, I, O, T, N, S, L, C. Prioritize guessing these letters early. Less common letters like Q, Z, X, and J should only be guessed after common letters have been eliminated. Most Wordle answers use common letters — uncommon letters appear rarely.</p>\n<h2>Deduction Process</h2>\n<p>After each guess, use the feedback systematically. Green letters are correct and in the right position — write them down. Yellow letters are in the word but wrong position — note their exclusion from those positions. Gray letters are not in the word at all — eliminate them from all future guesses.</p>\n<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reusing gray letters — once a letter is ruled out, never use it again</li>\n<li>Ignoring letter position — a yellow letter cannot go in the same position</li>\n<li>Not considering double letters — words can have repeated letters (e.g., BANANA)</li>\n<li>Guessing without elimination — narrow down possibilities before guessing</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Play Wordle Online Free</h2>\n<p><a href="/en/g/wordle">Play Wordle online free</a> on BrowserGamesHQ and apply these strategies to solve every daily puzzle.</p>'));

out.push(usecasePost('nitrotype-typing-speed-guide', 'Nitrotype Guide: How to Improve Your Typing Speed Fast', stableDate('nitrotype-typing-speed-guide'), 'Guides',
  'Complete Nitrotype guide to improve your typing speed. Learn proper technique, practice methods, and strategies to win races consistently.',
  '<p>Nitrotype combines typing practice with competitive racing, making skill improvement genuinely fun. This guide covers proper typing technique, effective practice methods, and race-winning strategies.</p>\n<img src="https://placehold.co/800x400/5f3dc4/ede9fe?text=Nitrotype+Guide" alt="Nitrotype typing guide" loading="lazy" style="max-width:100%;border-radius:8px;margin:16px 0">\n<h2>Proper Typing Technique</h2>\n<p><strong>Correct finger placement</strong> is the foundation of fast typing. Your left hand rests on A-S-D-F and your right hand on J-K-L-;. Each finger is responsible for specific keys. Touch typing (typing without looking at the keyboard) is essential for speed.</p>\n<h3>Finger Placement Guide</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Left pinky: Q, A, Z</li>\n<li>Left ring: W, S, X</li>\n<li>Left middle: E, D, C</li>\n<li>Left index: R, T, F, G, V, B</li>\n<li>Right index: Y, U, H, J, N, M</li>\n<li>Right middle: I, K</li>\n<li>Right ring: O, L</li>\n<li>Right pinky: P</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Accuracy First, Speed Second</h2>\n<p>The most common mistake new typists make is prioritizing speed over accuracy. <strong>Slow, accurate typing builds speed naturally.</strong> Each mistake requires backspace and retyping, which wastes more time than typing carefully. Focus on 100% accuracy first — speed will follow as muscle memory develops.</p>\n<h2>Practice Methods That Work</h2>\n<p>Structured practice produces faster improvement than casual typing. Use typing drills that target your weakest letter combinations. Most typists have specific letter pairs (like au, io, tr) that slow them down. Identify your weaknesses through practice and target them specifically.</p>\n<h3>Weekly Practice Plan</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Day 1-2: Focus on home row accuracy (A-S-D-F-J-K-L-;)</li>\n<li>Day 3-4: Practice top row letters (Q-W-E-R-T-Y-U-I-O-P)</li>\n<li>Day 5-6: Practice bottom row (Z-X-C-V-B-N-M)</li>\n<li>Day 7: Combine all rows in full-text practice</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Nitrotype Race Strategy</h2>\n<p>In Nitrotype races, consistency beats bursts of speed. A steady 60 WPM throughout the race beats a typist who does 80 WPM for the first half but makes mistakes in the second half. Focus on reading slightly ahead of where you are typing — this reduces hesitation between words.</p>\n<h2>Play Nitrotype Online Free</h2>\n<p><a href="/en/g/nitrotype">Play Nitrotype online free</a> on BrowserGamesHQ. Race against players worldwide and watch your typing speed improve with every race.</p>'));

